The latest stable version is **MSTest 4.2.3** (a major version jump from your 3.8.0). Here are the breaking changes relevant to **your code**:

### 🔴 `[ExpectedException]` is removed

Your two test methods use `[ExpectedException]`, which no longer exists in v4. Replace with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>`:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

### Other v3→v4 breaking changes (not in your code today, but good to know)

| Change | Impact |
|--------|--------|
| `Assert.ThrowsException` removed | Use `Assert.ThrowsExactly` instead |
| `Assert` APIs no longer accept `message` + `params object[]` | Use string interpolation for messages |
| `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed | Just use `[ClassCleanup]` (runs end-of-class now) |
| `TestTimeout` enum removed | Use `[Timeout(int.MaxValue)]` |
| `TestContext.Properties` is now `IDictionary<string, object>` | Use `.ContainsKey()` instead of `.Contains()` |
| `TestContext.ManagedType` removed | Use `FullyQualifiedTestClassName` |
| Custom `TestMethodAttribute.Execute` → `ExecuteAsync` | Override is now async |
| `TestMethodAttribute("name")` constructor changed | Use `DisplayName = "name"` property |
| `GenericParameterHelper` made internal | — |
| .NET < 8 support dropped | You're on net8.0, so you're fine |

